# keur quality control — a common misspelled Sonar property key.
#
# Why this exists: SonarQube/SonarCloud silently IGNORE unknown keys. A typo
# like `sonar.exclusion` (singular) or lowercase `sonar.projectkey` does not
# error — the setting simply has no effect, so your exclusions do not apply or
# the project key is unset, and you only notice when the dashboard looks wrong.
# This rule catches the frequent misspellings directly.
#
# HOW (pattern engine): match the known-bad key spellings at the start of a
# line. Each is a real spelling people hit (singular vs plural, wrong case,
# reportPath vs reportPaths).
#
# WARN: a typo'd key is almost always a mistake, but a future Sonar key could
# look similar, so it warns rather than blocks. @see docs/rules-authoring.md
id: SONAR-004
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 3
title: Misspelled sonar property key (silently ignored by Sonar)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: warn
confidence: 0.7
target:
  filenames: sonar-project.properties
  content_contains: sonar.
patterns:
  - regex: (?m)^\s*sonar\.exclusion\s*=
    message: "`sonar.exclusion` is not a Sonar key (it is `sonar.exclusions`, plural) — this line is silently ignored and nothing is excluded."
  - regex: (?m)^\s*sonar\.projectkey\s*=
    message: "`sonar.projectkey` has the wrong case — the key is `sonar.projectKey` (camelCase). Sonar ignores the misspelled line, leaving the project key unset."
  - regex: (?m)^\s*sonar\.(javascript|typescript|python|go|php|ruby)\.coverage\.reportPath\s*=
    message: "Coverage key is `...reportPaths` (plural). The singular `reportPath` is ignored and coverage reads 0%."
fix: "Correct the key spelling: `sonar.exclusions` (plural), `sonar.projectKey` (camelCase), `...coverage.reportPaths` (plural). Unknown keys are silently dropped by Sonar, so a typo has no effect and no error."
